From e3f4e18fde783cc598997f697a9b059a8bef3ebb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jetson <jetson@orin-nano.tail52323b.ts.net>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:34:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] nv_attach: per-thread map model prototype (thread-local,
 sum and device per-thread maps)

Prototype of the per-thread map model (branch proto/map-model, not for
upstream). Correctness rests on documented guarantees only (step0b): local
memory is the thread's own for the kernel's run, atomics are atomic, writes
of a completed kernel are visible after synchronization.

- 1530 thread-local array: each GPU thread's copy lives in a kernel-scope
  .local area the agent adds to every probed kernel (zeroed when the kernel
  starts); its cvta.local address is passed to the probe functions
  (nv_thread_local_routing.cpp). Lookups with a constant map fd become the
  address (key bounds checked); other map helper calls get it as eBPF r5,
  0 from probe functions no routed kernel calls. The CPU sees no values.
- 1531 sum array: u64 counters in device memory, changed with atomic adds
  only, spread over (SM, lane) shards (an add into one global word per
  bucket cost 1.07 ns per thread on empty kernels, the (SM, lane) shards
  0.16 ns with the carry); the CPU sees each word summed over the shards.
- 1532 device per-thread array: 1502's layout in device memory, atomic adds
  only.
- Delivery (agent): a thread of its own (relaxed capture mode, own stream)
  runs a snapshot kernel that reads every word with ld.relaxed.gpu (morally
  strong with the programs' gpu-scope atom.add: no data race) and sums the
  shards into pinned staging memory, synchronizes its stream, then copies
  into the shared values; every 20 ms while values change, else 200 ms;
  a final delivery at exit (atexit). Keys max_entries + 0..2 of 1531/1532
  read the status: deliveries, final delivery done, pid.

Checked on a victim with predicated exits, partial warps and graph replays
(entry/exit carry of the thread index: 0 mismatches over 3.88M thread
executions; histogram and per-thread counts exact) and on llama.cpp pp512
(four kernels: exit counts exactly 3x step 0's per-run counts after a
warmup and two runs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
